---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Accessibility statement" description="Accessibility of the Nazir and Company website: aims, testing and how to report a problem.">
  <header class="page-head w">
    <span class="eb">Accessibility</span>
    <h1 class="h h--xl">Accessibility Statement</h1>
  </header>
  <section class="sec--tight page-body">
    <div class="w prose">
      <p>The website aims to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at level AA.</p>
      <h2>What has been done</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Every page is tested with automated accessibility checks (axe) and has no known violations.</li>
        <li>Text contrast is at least 4.5:1, including text set over photographs, which sits on a dark gradient.</li>
        <li>All functions work with a keyboard, focus is always visible, and a “Skip to content” link is provided.</li>
        <li>Pages work at 200% text zoom and on screens from 320 pixels wide, with no sideways scrolling.</li>
        <li>Motion is limited to short hover and focus transitions; nothing moves on its own, and transitions are switched off when the device asks for reduced motion.</li>
        <li>The project list is a standard table that works without JavaScript; filters add to it but are not required. Carousels and tabs show their first item without JavaScript and never advance on their own.</li>
        <li>Maps have text alternatives, and every country shown on a map is also given in a list. Photographs have text alternatives or are marked as decorative.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Known limitations</h2>
      <p>Downloadable PDF documents are generated automatically and are not fully tagged for screen readers. The same information is available on the website pages.</p>
      <h2>Report a problem</h2>
      <p>Use the <a href="/contact/">enquiry form</a> and choose “Other”.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
